  <prompt>Per FR-B3, route the user-upload "Save to Spaarke" path (`OfficeService` / `OfficeDocumentPersistence`) through the SAME engine as capture so a hand-filed email gets association + triage + provenance identically to a mailbox-captured email, and shares the same dedup: message-level on internet-message-id (FR-C1 / task 021) and attachment content-hash (FR-C3 / task 024). This resolves the capture-vs-upload two-path problem — a saved email becomes an intelligence-bearing `sprk_communication`, not merely an archived `sprk_document`.</prompt>
  <role>SPAARKE platform developer with Communication capture-pipeline + Office upload + SPE dedup expertise. Follow ADR-045 (extend never fork), ADR-013 (AI facade), ADR-007 (SpeFileStore), ADR-038 (seam tests), and BFF §10 hygiene strictly.</role>
  <goal>A user-saved email is associated + triaged by the engine (not merely archived as `sprk_document`) and is deduped against capture and other users via internet-message-id (FR-C1), with attachment content-hash dedup via FR-C3. One code path; no separate upload-only archive branch. BFF publish size ≤60 MB with delta reported.</goal>

  <context>
    <background>FR-B3 (spec §Requirements Pillar B) + plan Phase 4 B3. The spec Executive Summary names "the capture-vs-upload split" as one of the two structural gaps. `Services/Office/OfficeService.cs` + `OfficeDocumentPersistence.cs` currently archive a saved email as a `sprk_document` without the engine. This task makes upload a peer entry into the capture engine, sharing FR-C1 message-id dedup + FR-C3 attachment content-hash dedup.</background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file role="modify">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Office/OfficeService.cs</file>
      <file role="modify">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Office/OfficeDocumentPersistence.cs</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Communication/IncomingCommunicationProcessor.cs</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Infrastructure/Graph/SpeFileStore.cs</file>
      <file role="test">tests/integration/seam/Communication/ (upload-vs-capture parity + dedup seam test)</file>
    </relevant-files>
    <dependencies>
      <dependency task="021" status="pending">FR-C1 — canonical internet-message-id dedup + Dataverse alternate key; the upload path reuses it (no second dedup mechanism).</dependency>
      <dependency task="024" status="pending">FR-C3 — SPE content dedup Tier-1 (`sprk_canonicalhash` = quickXorHash) on `SpeFileStore`; the email-attachment upload path hooks it.</dependency>
    </dependencies>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="ADR-045">Route upload into the EXISTING engine (`IncomingCommunicationProcessor` capture path) — do NOT fork a second engine or keep a separate archive-only branch; regarding via `RegardingFieldMap` (ADR-024) — scope: upload flow.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-013">AI/triage reached ONLY via `Services/Ai/PublicContracts/`; MUST NOT inject `IOpenAiClient`/`IPlaybookService`/node executors into Office/upload code — scope: upload triage.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-007">Attachment content-hash dedup reads `quickXorHash`/hash ONLY through the `SpeFileStore` facade (reuse FR-C3's detector) — do NOT call Graph directly from OfficeService — scope: attachment dedup.</constraint>
    <constraint source="NFR-02">Message-level dedup relies on the FR-C1 Dataverse alternate key (structural), not an app-level check-then-insert in the upload path — scope: upload dedup.</constraint>
    <constraint source="NFR-04">Upload capture is best-effort/non-fatal — engine/dedup/hash failures MUST NOT fail the user's save — scope: upload handler.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">BFF §10: state Placement Justification in the PR; `dotnet publish -c Release` + report absolute compressed size + delta vs baseline (~45.9 MB excl PDBs); no new HIGH CVE; update `tests/unit/Sprk.Bff.Api.Tests/` — scope: this BFF task.</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <knowledge>
    <topic>Unify upload with capture + shared dedup</topic>
    <files>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-045-communication-architecture.md</file>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-013-ai-architecture.md</file>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-007-spefilestore.md</file>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-024-polymorphic-resolver-pattern.md</file>
