      <file>docs/architecture/communication-service-architecture.md</file>
      <file>.claude/constraints/bff-extensions.md</file>
    </files>
    <patterns>
      <pattern name="Capture pipeline entry" location="src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Communication/IncomingCommunicationProcessor.cs">Upload MUST enter the same engine here so association+triage+provenance match mailbox capture.</pattern>
      <pattern name="SpeFileStore dedup hook" location="src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Infrastructure/Graph/SpeFileStore.cs">Reuse the FR-C3 content-hash detector on the email-attachment upload path via the facade.</pattern>
    </patterns>
  </knowledge>

  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="0" name="Context + rigor declaration">Load this POML + project CLAUDE.md + spec FR-B3 + FR-C1/C3 + BFF §10; declare RIGOR LEVEL FULL with reason per CLAUDE.md §8. Run `/conflict-check` on `Services/Communication/**` + `Services/Office/**`.</step>
    <step order="1">Read `OfficeService.cs` + `OfficeDocumentPersistence.cs` to map the current archive-only save path; read `IncomingCommunicationProcessor.cs` for the engine entry contract (what a captured email needs).</step>
    <step order="2">Re-route the "Save to Spaarke" upload so the saved email enters the same engine (association + triage + provenance) — producing a `sprk_communication`, not merely a `sprk_document` archive.</step>
    <step order="3">Wire message-level dedup: reuse FR-C1's internet-message-id alternate key so an upload that duplicates a captured/other-user email merges to the single canonical row (structural, NFR-02).</step>
    <step order="4">Wire attachment content-hash dedup: hook FR-C3's `SpeFileStore` detector on the email-attachment upload path (notify never silent).</step>
    <step order="5">Ensure the whole upload capture is non-fatal (NFR-04) — a triage/dedup/hash failure does not fail the user's save.</step>
    <step order="6">Add a seam test under `tests/integration/seam/Communication/` proving upload-vs-capture parity (identical engine output for the same email) + dedup (upload duplicating a capture → one canonical row; byte-identical attachment → no second canonical document). Update `tests/unit/Sprk.Bff.Api.Tests/`.</step>
    <step order="7">Run `dotnet publish -c Release`; record absolute compressed size + delta; `dotnet list package --vulnerable --include-transitive` (no new HIGH). Write Placement Justification into task notes for the PR.</step>
    <step order="8">Update TASK-INDEX.md: set this task's status to ✅.</step>
    <step order="9">Document any deviation in projects/email-communication-intelligence-r2/notes/.</step>
  </steps>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>If FR-C1 (task 021) or FR-C3 (task 024) is not yet merged, do NOT re-implement a second dedup mechanism in the upload path to "unblock" — STOP and escalate per CLAUDE.md §6; the whole point (NFR-02/NFR-09) is one dedup authority. If the engine entry contract cannot accept an upload-sourced email without a shape change, surface it as an ADR-045 tension (CLAUDE.md §6.5) rather than forking.</trigger>
  </escalation>

  <justification>OMIT — modify-only re-routing of the existing `OfficeService`/`OfficeDocumentPersistence` upload path onto the existing engine (021) + existing dedup detectors (021/024). No new component/endpoint/DI/column introduced by this task.</justification>

  <tools>
    <tool name="dotnet">Build/test the BFF; publish for size measurement.</tool>
  </tools>

  <outputs>
    <output type="code">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Office/OfficeService.cs</output>
    <output type="code">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Office/OfficeDocumentPersistence.cs</output>
    <output type="test">tests/integration/seam/Communication/ (upload parity + dedup seam test)</output>
  </outputs>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">Given a user-saved email, when saved via "Save to Spaarke", then it is associated + triaged by the engine and produces a `sprk_communication` (not merely a `sprk_document` archive).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Given the same email saved by a user AND captured from a mailbox, when both processed, then exactly one canonical `sprk_communication` results (deduped on internet-message-id via FR-C1, structural).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Given byte-identical attachment content uploaded twice (any path), when persisted, then no second canonical `sprk_document` is created (FR-C3 Tier-1) and the user is notified (never silent).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative: an engine/dedup/hash failure during upload is non-fatal (NFR-04) — the user's save still completes and does not surface an unhandled error.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Upload and mailbox capture produce identical engine output for the same email (parity seam test green).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">BFF publish size ≤60 MB compressed with delta reported; no new HIGH CVE; tests in `tests/unit/Sprk.Bff.Api.Tests/` updated. All unit tests pass; build is green. TASK-INDEX.md ✅; deviations recorded under notes/.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>Spec refs: FR-B3, FR-C1, FR-C3, NFR-02/04/09, Success Criterion 3 + 4. Depends on 021 (C1) + 024 (C3). `/conflict-check` before the PR (contended Services/Communication + Services/Office). Completion summary appended here when done.

ABSORBS FR-B1 mechanism-2 (2026-08-05, from task 041 Option A re-scope): the add-in **drag target** → identical engine output is the SAME unification this task performs — routing the add-in/user-upload save (`/api/office/save` → `OfficeService`/`OfficeDocumentPersistence`, today a `sprk_document`-only path) through the Association Engine so a dragged/dropped email yields association + triage + provenance identical to mailbox capture, deduped on the same keys. Add the add-in drop wiring (`src/client/office-addins/shared/taskpane/hooks/useSaveFlow.ts` — keep the call on `authenticatedFetch` per task 040) as part of this task's client surface, and add a seam test proving add-in-drop → engine parity. (FR-B1 mechanism-1 — the shared monitored intake folder — is already delivered by existing receive-enabled-account config; see docs/guides/COMMUNICATION-ADMIN-GUIDE.md.)

